At the time the DEC 3000-500 hit the market, the largest (SCSI) disks 
were 500MB - 1GB. I suggest you find a smaller disk - preferably 2GB or 
less and try the installation again. The boot disk is usually more 
critical than other disks.
Have you read the SPD, the Release Notes or the Installation guide of 
the OSF/1 version you are installing? There should be notes about the 
supported hardware.
Another possible unsupported device is the Plextor CD-ROM.

When you succeed to boot the kernel and start the installation script, 
the machine itself and the native hardware shouldn't be a problem. 
Neither the firmware.

Look for a RZ25 (426MB) or RZ26 (1.05GB) to use as a system disk.


Kari







