It's been over 20 years since I used RSTS/E, but doesn't the BASIC-PLUS
RTS reside in the upper 16K of the user address space?  If so, then  you're
stuck.

Do you really need BASIC-PLUS?  Compiling under BP2 (or CSPCOM, which
should be on your system for free) and using the "disappearing RSX RTS" will
give you the full 32K (or maybe just 28K; I have a vague recollection that the
disappearing RTS still consumed 4K). 

