What might help is this: use a soft cloth and a little glycerine (or
water) and polish the cd (always radially).
Use the unix dd command to transfer the contents to disk. This works
quite often.
Another alternative is to use a DVD drive to make an image copy of the
cd. Perhaps a Blue Ray drive works even better, haven't tried that.
An old Tru64 V5.1B cd was unreadable on my Alpha's but Nero managed to
create an imagefile on a pc. Burning a cd from it produced a working
installation disk again.
