Hello All

As I have become the proud owner of a faulty BA23 power supply, I have
decided the time has come to design a modern replacement, for myself
and for the PDP11/MicroVAX community, and anyone else with the same
problem.

The end result of my little project would be a 1:1 replica of the
H7864-B power supply, housing a modern, more efficient PSU inside,
which surpasses the original specifications =96 easily done these days.

Instead of buying a refurbished, 25 or 30 year old unit for $300, a
bran new replacement would be available for less, and would be
guaranteed to work =96 better.

As I intend to spend some time and money on this project, I would
appreciate your feedback and opinion:

- Do you have the H7864 schematics or at least detailed signal and
pinout descriptions (I have what is available in the DEC maintenance
manuals, I need more details =96 esp. the LTC signal spec)
- Do you have any other comment, suggestion or request before I go
ahead (a counter-suggestion saying the whole thing is a waste of time
is also valuable input)

My apologies for the multiple postings.

Thanks,
-Alon.


