I'm trying to troubleshoot a couple of TK50 tape units. What I got is:
- one complete TK50 unit
- one TK50 unit which was missing the tape leader (the arrow sahped
one inside the unit)
- one CompacTape cartridge with unknown content
- one CompacTape cartridge with missing (ripped off) tape leader (the
eye shaped one in the tape) and unknown content

for both tape units I already cleaned with alcohol the magnetic head,
and removed the dust.

the first question is about the missing tape leaders (both the unit
and the cartridge one). I saw that they are sold on ebay, but they
seem a bit expensive (15=80 plus shipping). Having seen that the actual
pieces seem to be very simple, I was wondering if someone already
tried to reconstruct them. I actually already did an attempt with the
unit leader using a thin plastic sheet, and the unit was at least able
to begin loading the tape in the inner reel. Did anyone don something
similar and has some hints?

I did some attempts to load (at hardware level, I did not attempt to
actually read the data) the good tape cartridge in both unit. Here the
behaviour left me puzzled: in both units, tha tape began being loaded
in the inner reel, but the device soon signaled an error stae (green
led off, red led rapidly flashing). in both cases, I could not manage
to make the units rewing completely the tape: starting the unload
procedure (reported on the unit handle) resulted in having the tape
loaded further in the inner reel. What could be causing this? Could
the tape magnetic state be involved (I mean, if the tape was
demagnetized, would it affect the loading)? I saw that there are light
sensors involved, so I fear it is not the case, and this leaves only
the "both units broken" option.. Are TK50 units known for being easily
faulty?

thanks in advance for your help

Enrico


