If you can find an original take-up leader for 15�, do buy it, because 
it is the only way you can get it working correctly. Don't attempt to 
fix a broken take-up leader. The shape and measurements has to be 
exactly correct and the holes as well. Also the material is important 
for the reliable function.

I assume that your tests don't work as expected, because of the 
non-original take-up leader. That is one of the cases when the tape 
doesn't load to BOT (Beginning-of-tape).

I recommend that you buy the take-up leader and then test more.

The magnetic state of the (new/demagnetized/used) shouldn't affect the 
load procedure.

TK50's do last long (years) when used normally.



Kari




