Hello.
Are you in Italy? Where?
I successfully repaired more than one TK50 unit, replacing the
original tape-leader with an hand-made, using an X-Ray print as
plastic sheet.
The tape leader MUST be black, with the particularly shaped hole in
the center to signal to the drive the loading operation.
About the tape content, if you have a tape that has been written
previously with an higher density device (TK70), the TK50 cannot load
it succesfully,
because it doesn't recognize the alignment tracks nor the tape format.
In this case you need to bulk-erase the tape before the use.
If the tape have been formatted on TK50, no problem so far.
If the tape is new/erased, the drive will write automatically the
alignment tracks at the first load.
Good luck!
Andrea


